      "message": "[error] Line 101: 🔴 `reactionsUpdated()` removed the main-thread hop and now only uses `assert(Thread.isMainThread)`. In release builds, `assert` is stripped, so any off-main caller will mutate `@Published` state from a background thread, which can cause SwiftUI/Combine threading violations and flaky UI updates. Make main-thread execution guaranteed (e.g., mark the type/method `@MainActor` or explicitly dispatch to main when needed) instead of debug-only enforcement.",
